A||||3||SCCA FIERO||Side scoops. Who has em?||||5||
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||03-11-2000||08:19 PM||||Today I was removing my notchback to install a fastback clip. As I tried to romove the moldings I broke the panel that these (Mecham?) scoops replace so I fugured I may as well get a set since I want some anyway. I notice Fiero Store sells some (Too expensive) and Fiero Heaven sells some too(take forever to get them?). Who else sells them and at a descent price and speedy delivery? I also looked around for some open scoops without the ribs and can't find any. Does FOCOA sell those?<P>So who has scoops? (ribbed or open)<BR>Where did you get them?<BR>How was the quality of them?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||03-11-2000||08:23 PM||||If you are a member of FOCOA, they have THREE types of lower, rear quarter panels with scoops.  The ribbed style, and two open scoop style.<P>From the small picture on the latest Fiero Owner magazine, it looks like the "new" open scoop is just smaller in the opening area.  By that I mean it sticks out less.<P>$225 to members, if I remember correctly.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||Earne||03-11-2000||08:37 PM||||The new scoop looks a lot like this:<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=2238074&p=17431709&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=2238074&p=17431709&Sequence=2</A> <P>Phil saw them at Indiana show last year and asked about them.  Now they are in the FOCOA catalog and called P2000.  Sell for $225.  I haven't found a panel scoop yet the fits like the OEM panel.  I made these atarting with the panel that was on the car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||03-11-2000||11:40 PM||||RS Motorsports sells several Fiero sidescoops as well.||||reg||1
